WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.301
[♪ epic theme music playing]

2
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.452
[wind lightly whooshing]

3
00:02:05.292 --> 00:02:08.295
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

4
00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.972
[horse nickering]

5
00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:24.936
[horse nickering]

6
00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:28.273
[heavy doors open]

7
00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.538
[Rhaenyra] [echoing voice]
Helaena.

8
00:02:45.499 --> 00:02:46.875
Helaena.

9
00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:49.628
[voice clear]
Helaena.

10
00:02:50.796 --> 00:02:52.172
[gasps lightly]

11
00:02:57.886 --> 00:03:00.137
I'm sorry to disturb
your rest.

12
00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:02.640
Have you heard w-word
from my mother?

13
00:03:02.641 --> 00:03:04.058
No.

14
00:03:04.059 --> 00:03:06.061
Nor do I expect to. until...

15
00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.024
[birdsong]

16
00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:21.660
Did Aemond ask you
to ride into battle with him?

17
00:03:25.247 --> 00:03:26.664
Hm.

18
00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:28.250
Lord Corlys
imagined he would.

19
00:03:31.712 --> 00:03:34.005
When I was a girl.
I wanted to fly.

20
00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.175
But now. when...

21
00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.011
when I'm with Dreamfyre...

22
00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:45.434
it's...

23
00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:48.937
and then too much.

24
00:03:53.525 --> 00:03:57.111
I think our father
felt the same way.

25
00:03:57.112 --> 00:03:58.946
He renounced
the strength of dragons

26
00:03:58.947 --> 00:04:00.614
and embraced a quieter life.

27
00:04:00.615 --> 00:04:02.451
He did not wish
to be changed.

28
00:04:03.702 --> 00:04:07.956
You believe the dragons
alter us in some way?

29
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.918
You now have many dragons.

30
00:04:12.878 --> 00:04:15.297
Are you yourself not altered?

31
00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.716
[scoffs] No.

32
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.595
Well. I do not wish to be.

33
00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.932
I wished only
to put an end to our contest

34
00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.226
and restore us
to our proper order.

35
00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:30.645
[sighs]

36
00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.273
Helaena.

37
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.403
Sister. I believe that you...

38
00:04:39.613 --> 00:04:42.240
may be a dreamer.

39
00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:44.576
That you...

40
00:04:45.911 --> 00:04:47.245
see things.

41
00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.834
I see f-flashes sometimes.

42
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.837
Some cl-clearer
than others.

43
00:04:57.672 --> 00:04:59.257
What did you see last?

44
00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.470
A gray mare.

45
00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:07.432
Mm-hmm.

46
00:05:09.935 --> 00:05:12.103
What of Daemon?
Have you seen him?

47
00:05:14.606 --> 00:05:15.607
Hm?

48
00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.652
The Winter Wolves. then.

49
00:05:19.653 --> 00:05:21.363
Or Tumbleton.

50
00:05:22.948 --> 00:05:25.491
Will Ormund Hightower
be brought to heel?

51
00:05:25.492 --> 00:05:27.117
I don't know.

52
00:05:27.118 --> 00:05:29.788
You don't know?
Or you will not say?

53
00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.796
You may refuse me
as your sister.

54
00:05:38.797 --> 00:05:40.464
but I may compel you
as your queen.

55
00:05:40.465 --> 00:05:42.843
Now. tell me what you know!

56
00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:46.053
Tell me there has been
no mistake.

57
00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:48.013
that I will prevail.

58
00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.141
as the gods must surely intend.
Tell me.

59
00:06:03.405 --> 00:06:06.408
♪

60
00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.508
[grunting]

61
00:06:26.553 --> 00:06:27.721
[groaning]

62
00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:34.686
Mother.

63
00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:39.024
I told you I would come.
if I could.

64
00:06:41.276 --> 00:06:44.195
Were you not taken captive?

65
00:06:46.448 --> 00:06:47.866
Your sister was taken.

66
00:06:49.618 --> 00:06:51.620
But I managed
to stay hidden. to escape.

67
00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:56.708
You have been so clever
to remain here undiscovered.

68
00:06:58.209 --> 00:06:59.794
I thought all had
forsaken me.

69
00:07:02.047 --> 00:07:03.381
[sighs]

70
00:07:11.473 --> 00:07:13.099
How could I forsake...

71
00:07:13.892 --> 00:07:15.143
my best...

72
00:07:16.603 --> 00:07:18.063
and truest son?

73
00:07:20.565 --> 00:07:22.484
The city has fallen. Aemond.

74
00:07:24.569 --> 00:07:26.571
- [soft kiss]
- You're all I have left.

75
00:07:34.788 --> 00:07:36.623
[Alicent sighs]

76
00:07:39.584 --> 00:07:42.002
The road has been long
and perilous.

77
00:07:42.003 --> 00:07:43.421
so I'll be glad of a bed.

78
00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:47.634
What of Aegon?

79
00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:52.347
Aegon is most likely dead.

80
00:07:55.517 --> 00:07:57.102
I did all I could.

81
00:08:04.109 --> 00:08:05.443
And for you.

82
00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:14.368
[whispering]
But I have failed you. Aemond.

83
00:08:14.369 --> 00:08:15.370
No.

84
00:08:17.205 --> 00:08:19.289
- I was too young.
- Never.

85
00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.875
I was just a child.

86
00:08:22.961 --> 00:08:25.046
[sighs. sniffles]

87
00:08:57.746 --> 00:08:59.748
[Alicent moaning]

88
00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:11.842
And in this moment
I will give you a son.

89
00:09:11.843 --> 00:09:14.261
[Aemond moaning]

90
00:09:14.262 --> 00:09:15.722
Aemond.

91
00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.396
Aemond.

92
00:09:24.606 --> 00:09:26.608
- What have you seen?
- [gasps] Please.

93
00:09:39.704 --> 00:09:41.706
[creatures chittering]

94
00:09:43.541 --> 00:09:45.210
[footsteps approaching]

95
00:09:49.798 --> 00:09:51.299
Aemond.

96
00:09:54.761 --> 00:09:57.764
[♪ dramatic music playing]

97
00:10:23.331 --> 00:10:24.916
[Gwayne] Open the gates!

98
00:10:26.918 --> 00:10:28.920
[people chattering]

99
00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:36.469
[chattering continues]

100
00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.146
They've crossed
the Blackwater Rush.

101
00:10:47.147 --> 00:10:49.314
- How many?
- Twenty thousand.

102
00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:51.025
A day's march away.
Two at most.

103
00:10:52.944 --> 00:10:56.113
So. your dim
but ambitious Dornish friend

104
00:10:56.114 --> 00:10:57.615
died in the mud for nothing.

105
00:10:58.616 --> 00:10:59.783
That is no matter.

106
00:10:59.784 --> 00:11:01.451
I have a piece
on the board now

107
00:11:01.452 --> 00:11:03.121
that will bring the bitch
to her knees.

108
00:11:05.957 --> 00:11:07.458
And what is that?

109
00:11:14.549 --> 00:11:15.884
[sighs]

110
00:11:20.471 --> 00:11:22.473
[Caraxes bellowing]

111
00:11:24.684 --> 00:11:26.686
[whistling]

112
00:11:39.365 --> 00:11:41.367
[chittering]

113
00:11:44.537 --> 00:11:45.997
- My prince--
- Move!

114
00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.669
Where is she?
Where's Rhaena?

115
00:11:52.587 --> 00:11:54.880
I see we are dispensing
with courtesies.

116
00:11:54.881 --> 00:11:56.507
Is she here?

117
00:11:57.508 --> 00:12:01.595
She flew. just after
I sent to you.

118
00:12:01.596 --> 00:12:03.222
I could not hold her.

119
00:12:03.223 --> 00:12:05.934
Put her in chains
if you have to.
lock her in a cell.

120
00:12:07.185 --> 00:12:09.019
Do you imagine it's so easy
to force a dragonrider

121
00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.730
to do what she does not wish?

122
00:12:12.065 --> 00:12:13.357
She exposes me. too.

123
00:12:13.358 --> 00:12:15.359
She beseeched me
with tears in her eyes.

124
00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.362
swore that she would
remain here in hiding.

125
00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:22.032
Talk of a dragonrider
is rife in the Vale.

126
00:12:22.033 --> 00:12:24.618
The villagers gossip
of a wild girl in the mountains

127
00:12:24.619 --> 00:12:26.203
living amongst
nettles and sheep.

128
00:12:26.204 --> 00:12:28.288
I am finished
with the matter.

129
00:12:28.289 --> 00:12:30.082
It is in my best interest now
to alert the queen

130
00:12:30.083 --> 00:12:31.709
- to her flight.
- No.

131
00:12:32.627 --> 00:12:34.211
You may blunt
Rhaenyra's wrath.

132
00:12:34.212 --> 00:12:36.047
but you will not evade it.
Give me a day.

133
00:12:43.721 --> 00:12:45.139
Please.

134
00:12:48.601 --> 00:12:51.813
She has been here and there
seeking news of Vhagar.

135
00:12:53.481 --> 00:12:55.565
There's word of a sighting
near Fairmarket.

136
00:12:55.566 --> 00:12:57.277
so I can only assume...

137
00:13:01.656 --> 00:13:04.408
[dragon vocalizing]

138
00:13:04.409 --> 00:13:06.411
[Baela] We are two days
behind Aemond at best.

139
00:13:07.412 --> 00:13:10.290
I have long tired
of this endless searching.

140
00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:14.918
I cannot help but think
I'm being punished by Rhaenyra.

141
00:13:14.919 --> 00:13:16.963
or at least sent far
from her sight.

142
00:13:18.756 --> 00:13:21.092
She thinks of us
only as tools to be wielded.

143
00:13:22.844 --> 00:13:26.680
I wondered. my lady.
if I might beg you
for a kindness.

144
00:13:26.681 --> 00:13:29.933
My father wishes for Alyn
and me to be legitimized

145
00:13:29.934 --> 00:13:32.311
and take the Velaryon name.

146
00:13:32.312 --> 00:13:35.439
The queen
is being reluctant.

147
00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:37.275
You know my standing
after the Gullet.

148
00:13:38.151 --> 00:13:40.361
I do not think my words
would have much sway with her.

149
00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:43.990
But your father. perhaps.

150
00:13:45.158 --> 00:13:48.035
Why this concern now
with names and titles?

151
00:13:48.036 --> 00:13:50.329
- [dragon screeching]
- I understand your grievance.

152
00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.539
but surely. you have
a better thing in your dragon

153
00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.791
than any lordly appellation.

154
00:13:54.792 --> 00:13:57.044
It is only that
if either of us were to marry.

155
00:13:57.045 --> 00:13:59.296
That is...

156
00:13:59.297 --> 00:14:03.301
if either of us gained the favor
of some highborn lady.

157
00:14:04.344 --> 00:14:05.844
[scoffs]

158
00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:08.973
He has spoken to you. then.
Your brother.

159
00:14:12.977 --> 00:14:15.646
[dragons bellowing]

160
00:14:17.523 --> 00:14:19.233
Is it Vhagar?

161
00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:23.821
No.

162
00:14:24.364 --> 00:14:26.907
I did not think us like
to escape the Red Keep.

163
00:14:26.908 --> 00:14:29.660
But Ser Adrian remained
steadfast and resolute.

164
00:14:30.995 --> 00:14:33.330
He led us
to a secret gate. and--

165
00:14:33.331 --> 00:14:35.999
and I had enough coin
with me for horses.

166
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.834
We tried to remain
off the roads.

167
00:14:37.835 --> 00:14:41.880
but the forests have become
impassable in places.

168
00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:43.508
There are wild men
in the woods now.

169
00:14:44.384 --> 00:14:46.760
I would not have arrived here
if it wasn't for him.

170
00:14:46.761 --> 00:14:49.638
Rhaenyra took the castle.
but he remained loyal.

171
00:14:49.639 --> 00:14:51.723
He helped me at great risk
to his own person.

172
00:14:51.724 --> 00:14:53.434
He is a gr-- [gasps]

173
00:14:56.896 --> 00:14:58.272
Have I offended you?

174
00:15:03.111 --> 00:15:04.362
No.

175
00:15:10.868 --> 00:15:12.537
You are all I have left.

176
00:15:16.791 --> 00:15:19.127
- [footsteps receding]
- [sighs]

177
00:15:21.045 --> 00:15:23.047
[footsteps approaching]

178
00:15:28.386 --> 00:15:30.262
This is he.

179
00:15:30.263 --> 00:15:32.431
my protector and guide.
Ser Adrian.

180
00:15:32.432 --> 00:15:33.766
Your Grace.

181
00:15:37.812 --> 00:15:38.813
Mm.

182
00:15:45.111 --> 00:15:46.279
[sighs]

183
00:15:49.407 --> 00:15:52.410
Well. it seems
I owe you a debt.

184
00:15:55.163 --> 00:15:57.623
I did only
as my conscience demanded.

185
00:15:59.792 --> 00:16:02.086
The queen dowager
was treated shamefully.

186
00:16:13.431 --> 00:16:15.140
- [blade thwacking]
- [Alicent] Aemond!

187
00:16:15.141 --> 00:16:16.517
[gurgling]

188
00:16:17.977 --> 00:16:19.312
[body thuds]

189
00:16:24.442 --> 00:16:26.110
Sorry. Mother.

190
00:16:28.154 --> 00:16:31.491
There are secrets here.
and I can trust no stranger.

191
00:16:32.533 --> 00:16:34.452
[Alys] Ah. there you are.

192
00:16:36.287 --> 00:16:37.955
You're just in time
for supper.

193
00:16:42.126 --> 00:16:44.377
[liquid pouring]

194
00:16:44.378 --> 00:16:46.963
The maesters tell me
the fat of livestock

195
00:16:46.964 --> 00:16:48.673
is beneficial to the bones.

196
00:16:48.674 --> 00:16:51.635
But I do wonder how something
so slippery in substance

197
00:16:51.636 --> 00:16:54.514
can truly be benign.
[chuckles]

198
00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.183
Do try the wine. Lord Corlys.

199
00:16:58.184 --> 00:17:01.312
I find it wards off
the fetid air of this place.

200
00:17:03.523 --> 00:17:04.524
Mm.

201
00:17:06.734 --> 00:17:09.194
What are you about.
Hightower?

202
00:17:09.195 --> 00:17:11.822
Is this some kind
of final repast?

203
00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:15.325
Pigeon pie before
the executioner's block?

204
00:17:15.326 --> 00:17:16.661
On the contrary.

205
00:17:17.703 --> 00:17:19.579
We hope to enjoy
the pleasure of your company

206
00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.164
for quite some time.

207
00:17:21.165 --> 00:17:24.210
You will be of great assistance
to us in our little endeavor.

208
00:17:25.419 --> 00:17:28.714
- As what? A hostage?
- Hm.

209
00:17:29.882 --> 00:17:32.008
Does the savage queen
harbor such a tender heart

210
00:17:32.009 --> 00:17:34.052
that she should
cast away her crown

211
00:17:34.053 --> 00:17:35.679
for the sake of her
wayward Hand?

212
00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.014
I think not.

213
00:17:38.558 --> 00:17:40.684
The Velaryons. however.

214
00:17:40.685 --> 00:17:43.562
with their lord as forfeit.
the men of Driftmark

215
00:17:43.563 --> 00:17:46.648
will think better
of entering King's Landing.

216
00:17:46.649 --> 00:17:50.278
And without them.
the city will again
eat of its own disorder.

217
00:17:54.115 --> 00:17:56.199
H-How will that help

218
00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.369
when the Winter Wolves
are clawing at our gates?

219
00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:07.127
Do you know?

220
00:18:07.128 --> 00:18:10.297
More and more I am inclined

221
00:18:10.298 --> 00:18:11.757
to limit my diet...

222
00:18:13.301 --> 00:18:14.719
to the vegetable kingdom.

223
00:18:16.095 --> 00:18:18.014
Just as the people of Naathi do.

224
00:18:18.764 --> 00:18:21.099
If you have finished
with your instruction--

225
00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.893
What do you see in them. anyway?

226
00:18:23.894 --> 00:18:25.396
The Targaryen...

227
00:18:26.897 --> 00:18:28.064
element.

228
00:18:28.065 --> 00:18:29.816
You are a traveled man.

229
00:18:29.817 --> 00:18:32.111
you have seen
the world's wonders.

230
00:18:33.279 --> 00:18:35.614
Why limit yourself
in tedious alliance

231
00:18:35.615 --> 00:18:37.825
to the brutish
and the incurious?

232
00:18:41.454 --> 00:18:44.080
Your wife. of course.
was of their blood.

233
00:18:44.081 --> 00:18:46.292
That ended all too predictably.

234
00:18:49.128 --> 00:18:51.755
I would think.
after having seen

235
00:18:51.756 --> 00:18:53.799
how they devour
one of their own...

236
00:18:56.927 --> 00:18:58.638
I would like to return
to my cell.

237
00:18:59.847 --> 00:19:01.307
As you please.

238
00:19:05.603 --> 00:19:06.936
Oh. Lord Corlys?

239
00:19:06.937 --> 00:19:08.147
Before you go...

240
00:19:09.857 --> 00:19:11.776
He was in uncommon
good spirits...

241
00:19:12.902 --> 00:19:15.278
as though he were on the eve
of some great victory.

242
00:19:15.279 --> 00:19:17.614
He seems to believe that
with Lord Corlys as hos--

243
00:19:17.615 --> 00:19:19.367
Is this his
"piece on the board"?

244
00:19:21.118 --> 00:19:23.203
What does the order or disorder
of King's Landing

245
00:19:23.204 --> 00:19:25.455
matter to us now
with an army at the gates?

246
00:19:25.456 --> 00:19:27.375
I'm supposed to be the king.

247
00:19:29.627 --> 00:19:31.544
What sort of ruler am I?

248
00:19:31.545 --> 00:19:34.297
Am I to sit by impotent
while a madman

249
00:19:34.298 --> 00:19:35.966
offers us up
for the slaughter?

250
00:19:37.885 --> 00:19:39.804
And all of our men with us?

251
00:19:41.514 --> 00:19:43.182
Seems there's no escaping it.

252
00:19:44.266 --> 00:19:47.561
The dream some have
of covering themselves
in everlasting glory...

253
00:19:49.063 --> 00:19:51.399
of somehow transcending
humanity's common fate.

254
00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:58.656
I am sorry about your friend.

255
00:20:00.157 --> 00:20:01.991
[sniffling]

256
00:20:01.992 --> 00:20:04.078
He gave himself to the dust.

257
00:20:10.167 --> 00:20:12.001
I could order the army
to surrender.

258
00:20:12.002 --> 00:20:14.087
[scoffs]
And then what?

259
00:20:14.088 --> 00:20:16.006
Have us all marched
to the gallows?

260
00:20:18.676 --> 00:20:21.595
You could fly away
on Tessarion.

261
00:20:22.847 --> 00:20:24.222
Without you
as a pretext for--

262
00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:26.183
He would continue
as he began.

263
00:20:27.935 --> 00:20:29.978
Where would I go?

264
00:20:29.979 --> 00:20:33.190
Who would receive a king who
left his own men to their ruin?

265
00:20:36.402 --> 00:20:38.738
I have no fear
of insignificance. Gwayne.

266
00:20:42.742 --> 00:20:44.952
Rhaenyra may keep her crown.
for all I care.

267
00:20:47.246 --> 00:20:48.997
[chuckles softly]

268
00:20:48.998 --> 00:20:50.707
[Torrhen Manderly]
Frankly. it is outrageous.

269
00:20:50.708 --> 00:20:53.918
There is a campaign against me!
Jeering in the streets.

270
00:20:53.919 --> 00:20:57.213
My own daughter found
the doorstep of my city dwelling

271
00:20:57.214 --> 00:21:00.134
smeared with some sort of
foul matter.

272
00:21:01.844 --> 00:21:04.053
I don't know what you
want me to do about it.

273
00:21:04.054 --> 00:21:05.264
My queen.

274
00:21:06.098 --> 00:21:07.266
With respect.

275
00:21:08.601 --> 00:21:11.770
In front of petitioners.
you named me responsible

276
00:21:11.771 --> 00:21:15.148
for the current financial
grievances in the city.

277
00:21:15.149 --> 00:21:16.483
I hardly be--

278
00:21:16.484 --> 00:21:17.902
Well. what have you done
to alleviate them?

279
00:21:18.903 --> 00:21:21.738
What can I do?

280
00:21:21.739 --> 00:21:24.575
I have advocated for a tax.
It has fallen on deaf ears.

281
00:21:25.367 --> 00:21:29.496
Our dribbles of gold are spent
as fast as they are gathered.

282
00:21:29.497 --> 00:21:31.873
It's as if I have been
installed here

283
00:21:31.874 --> 00:21:33.918
as some sort of scapegoat.

284
00:21:38.255 --> 00:21:40.090
Has there been any word
from Lord Corlys?

285
00:21:41.967 --> 00:21:43.260
From Harrenhal?

286
00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:49.641
- And Daemon?
- [Orwyle] Absent.

287
00:21:49.642 --> 00:21:53.937
The prince is on some...
errand of his own.

288
00:21:53.938 --> 00:21:57.607
The Keepers say he flew out
of the city before dawn.

289
00:21:57.608 --> 00:21:59.609
The river host
are but a day's march

290
00:21:59.610 --> 00:22:01.277
from Tumbleton. Your Grace.

291
00:22:01.278 --> 00:22:03.863
and the Velaryon forces will be
at King's Landing on the morrow.

292
00:22:03.864 --> 00:22:07.200
I have a reputation
to uphold.

293
00:22:07.201 --> 00:22:10.161
If Ser Adrian
has been successful

294
00:22:10.162 --> 00:22:12.789
in his endeavor. of course.

295
00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:15.458
then there is the small matter
of Harrenhal--

296
00:22:15.459 --> 00:22:17.711
Just take it.

297
00:22:18.671 --> 00:22:20.296
Your Grace?

298
00:22:20.297 --> 00:22:22.465
Return to the Twins

299
00:22:22.466 --> 00:22:25.844
and lead the men you have
left there to Harrenhal.

300
00:22:25.845 --> 00:22:27.679
[gasps]

301
00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:29.973
This I will do gladly!

302
00:22:29.974 --> 00:22:31.933
If Aemond is dead.
all the better.

303
00:22:31.934 --> 00:22:34.060
But in any case.
you shall occupy it again.
and leave no place

304
00:22:34.061 --> 00:22:35.228
- for him to return.
- [door opens]

305
00:22:35.229 --> 00:22:37.064
- [Addam] My queen.
- [footsteps approaching]

306
00:22:38.983 --> 00:22:40.984
We have seen
something strange.

307
00:22:40.985 --> 00:22:42.569
- Vhagar?
- No.

308
00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:44.654
Sheepstealer.
In the Riverlands.

309
00:22:44.655 --> 00:22:46.574
on the banks of the Blue Fork
near Fairmarket.

310
00:22:47.575 --> 00:22:49.242
That is unexpected.
He's not known--

311
00:22:49.243 --> 00:22:51.036
Your Grace. he has a rider.

312
00:22:52.329 --> 00:22:55.081
- A new rider?
- I could not say.

313
00:22:55.082 --> 00:22:57.333
We gave chase.
but lost him in the hills.

314
00:22:57.334 --> 00:22:59.336
[high-pitch ringing.
sounds muffling]

315
00:23:02.548 --> 00:23:04.591
That head
Daemon brought to you.

316
00:23:04.592 --> 00:23:06.759
can you say in honesty
you've had no doubts?

317
00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.762
He was long in the Riverlands.
and now Sheepstealer

318
00:23:09.763 --> 00:23:12.765
is sighted there with a rider
he assured you was dead.

319
00:23:12.766 --> 00:23:14.726
And in that same moment.

320
00:23:14.727 --> 00:23:17.395
he has absented himself
without explanation.

321
00:23:17.396 --> 00:23:19.647
I have known him to lie.
but this is a great--

322
00:23:19.648 --> 00:23:22.775
You and I have known him to be
capable of far worse than lies.

323
00:23:22.776 --> 00:23:25.069
He has chafed
since you arrived here

324
00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:27.071
over your restraint
in wielding power.

325
00:23:27.072 --> 00:23:29.324
He is impetuous
and impatient.

326
00:23:29.325 --> 00:23:31.743
Who can say what alliance
he may have formed in secret

327
00:23:31.744 --> 00:23:34.914
- when he found you lacking.
- He has sworn to serve me.

328
00:23:36.248 --> 00:23:38.625
I cannot believe that now.
when I need him most.

329
00:23:38.626 --> 00:23:40.085
- that he would--
- Forgive me.

330
00:23:45.215 --> 00:23:46.383
Your Grace.

331
00:23:50.054 --> 00:23:52.096
But is there anything
Daemon could do

332
00:23:52.097 --> 00:23:54.308
that you would truly
not believe?

333
00:23:59.229 --> 00:24:00.898
Fetch Ser Addam.

334
00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:11.491
They say it is the strength
of the sun in Volantis

335
00:24:11.492 --> 00:24:13.410
that makes for such sweetness
in the grape.

336
00:24:14.912 --> 00:24:17.163
If you mean to console me
for this folly

337
00:24:17.164 --> 00:24:19.666
with Volantene wines.
you're much mistaken.

338
00:24:19.667 --> 00:24:22.335
Your Grace.
I beg you. reconsider.

339
00:24:22.336 --> 00:24:25.338
At Maidenpool.
we might take ship
for Casterly Rock instead.

340
00:24:25.339 --> 00:24:27.799
[Aegon]
No. I am decided on Braavos.

341
00:24:27.800 --> 00:24:29.926
How much further
must we ride?

342
00:24:29.927 --> 00:24:31.428
Some days still to the port.

343
00:24:32.429 --> 00:24:34.514
Braavos will prove itself
a most cultivated city.

344
00:24:34.515 --> 00:24:36.474
- I assure you.
- [pig squealing]

345
00:24:36.475 --> 00:24:38.017
Perhaps even
a home from home.

346
00:24:38.018 --> 00:24:39.478
[pig squealing]

347
00:24:42.690 --> 00:24:43.774
Whoa.

348
00:24:44.525 --> 00:24:47.318
My good woman.
what is it you flee?

349
00:24:47.319 --> 00:24:48.987
An army marches this way.

350
00:24:48.988 --> 00:24:51.280
- Some thousand strong.
- Which army?

351
00:24:51.281 --> 00:24:53.866
My daughter said she saw
the red fish on the white.

352
00:24:53.867 --> 00:24:56.452
- The Mootons.
- That's where we are going.
to Maidenpool.

353
00:24:56.453 --> 00:24:59.122
We must keep moving.
Turn back if you can.

354
00:24:59.123 --> 00:25:00.624
Mootons are sworn to Rhaenyra.

355
00:25:02.126 --> 00:25:03.711
They can't have
heard about me?

356
00:25:06.005 --> 00:25:07.046
Hyah.

357
00:25:07.047 --> 00:25:10.050
[♪ dramatic music playing]

358
00:25:12.845 --> 00:25:14.847
[distant people chattering]

359
00:25:16.974 --> 00:25:18.475
[Tyland]
The road is lost to us.

360
00:25:19.476 --> 00:25:21.978
We must fall back
to Rook's Rest.

361
00:25:21.979 --> 00:25:24.480
We can't go back there.
We may have been discovered.

362
00:25:24.481 --> 00:25:27.317
There is an army coming for us
and we have no place to shelter.

363
00:25:28.736 --> 00:25:30.069
There are thick walls
at Rook's Rest

364
00:25:30.070 --> 00:25:31.696
and enough men
to defend them.

365
00:25:31.697 --> 00:25:34.825
It shall be refuge for His Grace
till Mooton's host has passed.

366
00:25:36.827 --> 00:25:39.704
[utensils clacking]

367
00:25:39.705 --> 00:25:41.665
- [Aemond] Mm.
- [Alys] You must be famished.

368
00:25:43.083 --> 00:25:45.044
It's a long journey
from King's Landing.

369
00:25:47.504 --> 00:25:48.505
Yes.

370
00:25:50.507 --> 00:25:51.884
And fraught. no doubt.

371
00:25:53.343 --> 00:25:55.429
If half the tales I have heard
about the King's Road are true.

372
00:25:59.016 --> 00:26:01.350
How is it that the two of you

373
00:26:01.351 --> 00:26:04.229
- came to know one another?
- Mm.

374
00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:08.358
She saved my life.

375
00:26:10.527 --> 00:26:12.195
At whose behest?

376
00:26:12.196 --> 00:26:14.030
Your lord's?

377
00:26:14.031 --> 00:26:15.866
I generally follow
my own dictates.

378
00:26:18.535 --> 00:26:21.245
[laughing] Aemond. I still don't
understand who this woman is.

379
00:26:21.246 --> 00:26:23.122
[sighs]

380
00:26:23.123 --> 00:26:24.249
Mm.

381
00:26:25.542 --> 00:26:27.544
She is a lady.

382
00:26:29.088 --> 00:26:30.881
And a maester. of sorts.

383
00:26:33.092 --> 00:26:35.928
The care of the castle
has fallen to her for now.

384
00:26:38.388 --> 00:26:41.766
I've decided
to stay here with her

385
00:26:41.767 --> 00:26:43.393
and make this place my seat.

386
00:26:45.979 --> 00:26:47.772
Your seat?

387
00:26:47.773 --> 00:26:49.775
Was that not what you
yourself suggested?

388
00:26:51.068 --> 00:26:52.819
A new fortress
from which to rule.

389
00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:56.697
Rhaenyra has the throne
and six dragons to her name.

390
00:26:56.698 --> 00:26:59.909
It is she who rules now.
as much as we
might wish it otherwise.

391
00:26:59.910 --> 00:27:01.119
Mm.

392
00:27:01.120 --> 00:27:04.832
Rhaenyra's dragons
are ridden by commoners.

393
00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:10.419
She's defiled our great house.
diminished the Iron Throne.

394
00:27:10.420 --> 00:27:12.422
and sowed the seeds
of her own ruin.

395
00:27:14.091 --> 00:27:15.592
She will certainly fail.

396
00:27:18.137 --> 00:27:20.806
And we will raise
our own throne.

397
00:27:22.516 --> 00:27:25.602
In the mud of the Riverlands.

398
00:27:27.688 --> 00:27:29.189
A new dawn is coming.

399
00:27:32.109 --> 00:27:34.319
A new line of unsullied kings.

400
00:27:37.656 --> 00:27:39.366
We need only to bide our time.

401
00:27:41.785 --> 00:27:43.287
And you. Mother.

402
00:27:45.164 --> 00:27:46.957
You will wait with us.

403
00:27:48.458 --> 00:27:50.668
You have worth yet to offer.

404
00:27:50.669 --> 00:27:53.463
I'm sure your mother
will wish to move on.

405
00:27:54.882 --> 00:27:57.341
Back to Oldtown. perhaps.

406
00:27:57.342 --> 00:27:59.468
Our climate
doesn't seem to suit her.

407
00:27:59.469 --> 00:28:02.221
Mm. there's nothing
for her there.
I am all she has left.

408
00:28:02.222 --> 00:28:03.682
- [Alicent] There is Helaena.
- No!

409
00:28:04.516 --> 00:28:06.018
You'll stay with us.

410
00:28:10.898 --> 00:28:12.399
We're out of wood.

411
00:28:14.484 --> 00:28:16.195
[plate clattering]

412
00:28:20.199 --> 00:28:23.659
I will not be coddled
or admonished
like a witless child.

413
00:28:23.660 --> 00:28:25.829
Tread carefully
with her. Aemond.

414
00:28:26.914 --> 00:28:28.831
She's come to do you some ill.

415
00:28:28.832 --> 00:28:30.583
She is my blood.

416
00:28:30.584 --> 00:28:33.169
- [wood chopping]
- And thus without blemish?

417
00:28:33.170 --> 00:28:36.131
She's always had her secrets.
most of them poorly kept.

418
00:28:37.174 --> 00:28:40.927
My designs for our future
did not include your mother.

419
00:28:40.928 --> 00:28:42.346
And there is the truth of it.

420
00:28:43.305 --> 00:28:44.848
You want me for yourself.

421
00:28:46.934 --> 00:28:48.894
There is a fog
that surrounds her.

422
00:28:51.438 --> 00:28:53.899
She has come
to do you some evil.

423
00:28:55.525 --> 00:28:58.195
You would be wise to keep
your dark thoughts to yourself.

424
00:29:06.245 --> 00:29:09.248
You Targaryen boys all want
the same thing. don't you?

425
00:29:14.378 --> 00:29:16.380
[panting]

426
00:29:19.091 --> 00:29:20.384
[sniffling]

427
00:29:22.052 --> 00:29:24.054
[breathing heavily]

428
00:29:26.056 --> 00:29:29.059
[♪ dramatic music playing]

429
00:29:55.669 --> 00:29:57.796
- [panicked chatter]
- [baby crying]

430
00:30:01.258 --> 00:30:02.592
Tom Tangletongue. what news?

431
00:30:03.468 --> 00:30:06.762
Lord Mooton of Maidenpool.
he's dispatched an army.

432
00:30:06.763 --> 00:30:08.432
They're marching in haste.

433
00:30:09.850 --> 00:30:13.103
Have you not seen our Janos?
I thought he'd be with you.

434
00:30:14.104 --> 00:30:15.730
No. Where are they marching?

435
00:30:15.731 --> 00:30:17.940
They were commanded here.
to Rook's Rest.

436
00:30:17.941 --> 00:30:20.776
But they're going
village to village. it seems.

437
00:30:20.777 --> 00:30:22.863
in search
of your friend Lannister.

438
00:30:23.989 --> 00:30:26.199
Something about
the queen's gold.

439
00:30:26.908 --> 00:30:29.703
They'll be here
before w-we know it.
You'd best be on the move.

440
00:30:32.873 --> 00:30:34.124
[groaning]

441
00:30:35.208 --> 00:30:36.460
[grunting]

442
00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:43.299
I think you'll agree.
Ser Tyland.

443
00:30:43.300 --> 00:30:44.634
that you should
give yourself up.

444
00:30:45.469 --> 00:30:46.886
She will flay me alive.

445
00:30:46.887 --> 00:30:49.472
No doubt.
But once Mooton has you in hand.

446
00:30:49.473 --> 00:30:51.474
he'll turn towards
King's Landing.
and His Grace and I

447
00:30:51.475 --> 00:30:54.060
- may yet slip away.
- Give the king to me and my men.

448
00:30:54.061 --> 00:30:56.062
We will ride hard
and escape Mooton's clutches.

449
00:30:56.063 --> 00:30:58.064
Oh. must you be so thick?

450
00:30:58.065 --> 00:30:59.732
Rhaenyra is hunting you.

451
00:30:59.733 --> 00:31:01.859
His Grace is not safe
in your company.

452
00:31:01.860 --> 00:31:04.153
Turn yourself in
and give him the chance to flee.

453
00:31:04.154 --> 00:31:05.363
[Tyland] Him or you?

454
00:31:05.364 --> 00:31:07.365
[Larys]
It is the honorable thing to do.

455
00:31:07.366 --> 00:31:09.326
- Your Grace. for now. at least--
- No.

456
00:31:11.995 --> 00:31:13.412
No.

457
00:31:13.413 --> 00:31:15.040
Go where you will.

458
00:31:15.999 --> 00:31:17.209
Both of you.

459
00:31:18.251 --> 00:31:19.878
Preserve your own skins.

460
00:31:21.171 --> 00:31:22.755
But I shall run no more.

461
00:31:22.756 --> 00:31:24.840
If you do not run.
Your Grace. you will die.

462
00:31:24.841 --> 00:31:26.175
Then I'll die.

463
00:31:26.176 --> 00:31:27.844
But not as a fugitive.

464
00:31:30.180 --> 00:31:33.015
Unknown.
Covered in dust.

465
00:31:33.016 --> 00:31:37.687
Not with an arrow in my back
or trapped like a fox in a hole.

466
00:31:38.939 --> 00:31:41.023
This-- this is absurd.
Ser Tyland. I entreat you

467
00:31:41.024 --> 00:31:43.235
- to reason with His Grace.
- I'll make my stand here.

468
00:31:44.611 --> 00:31:46.780
Mm.
And be buried as a king.

469
00:31:48.448 --> 00:31:49.866
With my dragon.

470
00:31:53.662 --> 00:31:56.205
I will not have the histories
say that I was slain

471
00:31:56.206 --> 00:31:58.542
in ignominy
by my own brother.

472
00:32:04.881 --> 00:32:06.967
If the king wishes
to remain. then...

473
00:32:09.219 --> 00:32:11.053
I shall remain with him.

474
00:32:11.054 --> 00:32:13.140
I cannot leave him to face
an army meant for me.

475
00:32:16.226 --> 00:32:17.936
[horses neighing]

476
00:32:21.481 --> 00:32:23.233
You're resolved in this then?

477
00:32:30.574 --> 00:32:31.908
Well then. my lords...

478
00:32:33.410 --> 00:32:35.996
it seems there is only one thing
left for me to do.

479
00:32:37.497 --> 00:32:39.457
May the Seven
be ever at your side.

480
00:32:39.458 --> 00:32:41.459
[Tyland]
You would abandon
your master?

481
00:32:41.460 --> 00:32:43.795
I am a cripple. Ser Tyland.

482
00:32:45.922 --> 00:32:48.090
Humble enough to admit
that my presence in a fight

483
00:32:48.091 --> 00:32:49.634
would make
no earthly difference.

484
00:32:52.679 --> 00:32:55.098
Of course. if my king
commanded me to stay...

485
00:32:57.100 --> 00:32:58.810
What Lord Larys says is true.

486
00:33:00.854 --> 00:33:02.814
He would be no use to us here.

487
00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:05.108
Well. then.

488
00:33:06.860 --> 00:33:10.030
It will be my duty to see
that King Aegon is remembered.

489
00:33:11.990 --> 00:33:15.367
His heroic last hours
immortalized through story...

490
00:33:15.368 --> 00:33:16.995
- [chuckles softly]
- ...and song.

491
00:33:21.124 --> 00:33:22.459
Your Grace.

492
00:33:31.968 --> 00:33:33.637
[sighs]

493
00:33:36.473 --> 00:33:37.807
Your Grace.

494
00:33:38.892 --> 00:33:40.185
Come. come. come.

495
00:33:53.073 --> 00:33:55.075
[Sheepstealer bellowing]

496
00:33:59.162 --> 00:34:00.580
[screeching]

497
00:34:02.165 --> 00:34:04.417
[Caraxes whistling]

498
00:34:05.585 --> 00:34:07.587
[chittering]

499
00:34:10.006 --> 00:34:11.716
[bellowing]

500
00:34:19.349 --> 00:34:22.352
[dragons screeching.
bellowing]

501
00:34:30.860 --> 00:34:32.778
- Stay back!
- You swore to me.

502
00:34:32.779 --> 00:34:34.905
- You should not have come.
- Did you think she would
not hear of this?

503
00:34:34.906 --> 00:34:37.784
Stay back!
He does not heed me!

504
00:34:38.952 --> 00:34:41.037
[roaring]

505
00:34:42.414 --> 00:34:43.540
<i>Daor!</i>

506
00:34:45.083 --> 00:34:47.085
[screeching]

507
00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:49.963
<i>Daor!</i>

508
00:34:56.886 --> 00:34:59.096
What do you hope to do here?
In the reeds and the mud?

509
00:34:59.097 --> 00:35:00.806
Vhagar was here.

510
00:35:00.807 --> 00:35:02.266
Or near here. last I heard.

511
00:35:02.267 --> 00:35:03.809
We heard the same.
but she is gone.

512
00:35:03.810 --> 00:35:05.311
Then I will fly
in search of her.

513
00:35:05.312 --> 00:35:07.396
And if you find her?

514
00:35:07.397 --> 00:35:09.648
I thought I could do this.
but I can't.

515
00:35:09.649 --> 00:35:12.736
I cannot live the way I have.
cut off from all who loved me.

516
00:35:13.403 --> 00:35:15.780
And so. you think by going
after Vhagar. you will...

517
00:35:17.073 --> 00:35:18.240
what?

518
00:35:18.241 --> 00:35:19.950
If I kill her.

519
00:35:19.951 --> 00:35:21.910
I will have paid
some of my debt to Rhaenyra.

520
00:35:21.911 --> 00:35:24.121
I would at least have grounds
to sue for her mercy.

521
00:35:24.122 --> 00:35:26.248
- You will more likely die.
- Then I will have
paid all of it.

522
00:35:26.249 --> 00:35:28.627
I will die absolved
if I cannot live that way.

523
00:35:29.586 --> 00:35:31.588
[Sheepstealer roars]

524
00:35:38.595 --> 00:35:39.846
Let me help you. then.

525
00:35:41.431 --> 00:35:43.099
You cannot battle Vhagar alone.

526
00:35:44.309 --> 00:35:46.102
But the two of us
may yet prevail.

527
00:35:47.854 --> 00:35:49.439
Why would you do
such a thing?

528
00:35:51.107 --> 00:35:52.650
I had no dragon either
when I was young.

529
00:35:52.651 --> 00:35:53.777
Did you know that?

530
00:35:55.153 --> 00:35:57.863
My mother died in childbed
when I was three years of age.

531
00:35:57.864 --> 00:35:59.782
My brother sank into sadness.

532
00:35:59.783 --> 00:36:02.118
I was alone.
just as you have been.

533
00:36:05.955 --> 00:36:07.624
I should have done better.
Rhaena.

534
00:36:09.959 --> 00:36:11.961
[Caraxes whistling]

535
00:36:16.007 --> 00:36:18.967
- You lie.
- I did not summon them.

536
00:36:18.968 --> 00:36:22.304
- You'd betray your own daughter?
- I have not. I swear it.

537
00:36:22.305 --> 00:36:23.639
She does not yet know
who you are.

538
00:36:23.640 --> 00:36:25.557
[bellowing]

539
00:36:25.558 --> 00:36:26.725
[Daemon] Leave him.

540
00:36:26.726 --> 00:36:28.395
They will tear you
from the sky.

541
00:36:29.979 --> 00:36:31.146
[whimpering]

542
00:36:31.147 --> 00:36:32.857
Run! Run!

543
00:36:36.986 --> 00:36:38.655
[dragon roaring]

544
00:36:43.201 --> 00:36:45.578
[dragons bellowing]

545
00:36:47.414 --> 00:36:48.707
Go!

546
00:36:56.214 --> 00:36:58.216
[dragons vocalizing]

547
00:36:59.884 --> 00:37:01.886
[speaking High Valyrian]

548
00:37:03.513 --> 00:37:05.097
- Call off your dragon!
- What is your agreement

549
00:37:05.098 --> 00:37:08.225
with Sheepstealer's rider?
Answer carefully.

550
00:37:08.226 --> 00:37:10.227
You will not have
another chance to deceive me.

551
00:37:10.228 --> 00:37:11.729
I never wished to deceive you.

552
00:37:11.730 --> 00:37:13.564
- Then. speak!
- Call off your dragon.

553
00:37:13.565 --> 00:37:16.735
[dragons bellowing]

554
00:37:18.695 --> 00:37:20.529
[grunting]

555
00:37:20.530 --> 00:37:21.864
[Rhaena shouting]

556
00:37:21.865 --> 00:37:24.116
Please. Rhaenyra.

557
00:37:24.117 --> 00:37:25.535
She's not herself.

558
00:37:26.536 --> 00:37:28.538
- [Rhaena shouting]
- [dragons vocalizing]

559
00:37:39.758 --> 00:37:40.884
Rhaena?

560
00:37:45.972 --> 00:37:47.432
It wasn't you.

561
00:37:57.734 --> 00:38:00.402
She was Sheepstealer's rider?

562
00:38:00.403 --> 00:38:02.405
All this time. you knew.

563
00:38:07.076 --> 00:38:08.578
This is finished!

564
00:38:15.418 --> 00:38:18.129
[dragons roaring]

565
00:38:20.965 --> 00:38:21.966
Move!

566
00:38:23.259 --> 00:38:25.261
[roaring continues]

567
00:38:59.128 --> 00:39:00.546
[shouting in High Valyrian]

568
00:39:00.547 --> 00:39:02.549
[screeching]

569
00:39:12.392 --> 00:39:15.645
- Your Grace!
- Help Daemon! Go!

570
00:39:16.813 --> 00:39:17.896
Go!

571
00:39:17.897 --> 00:39:19.899
[dragons continue roaring]

572
00:39:23.987 --> 00:39:25.738
[Rhaenyra shouting]

573
00:39:30.994 --> 00:39:32.661
[gasping]

574
00:39:32.662 --> 00:39:33.830
With me!

575
00:39:39.711 --> 00:39:41.336
[screeching]

576
00:39:41.337 --> 00:39:42.755
No!

577
00:39:46.384 --> 00:39:48.386
[screeching continues]

578
00:39:51.431 --> 00:39:54.392
Escort the queen.
I will finish this.

579
00:40:09.407 --> 00:40:11.117
[screeching]

580
00:40:22.378 --> 00:40:24.087
[grunting]

581
00:40:24.088 --> 00:40:26.090
[Yelping. screeching]

582
00:40:30.929 --> 00:40:32.931
[grunting]

583
00:40:45.276 --> 00:40:46.903
[whimpers]

584
00:40:54.285 --> 00:40:57.079
[Mysaria]
It is magnificent in its way.

585
00:40:57.080 --> 00:41:00.500
[Madam Sylvi]
I saw it once before when
I petitioned the queen.

586
00:41:04.754 --> 00:41:07.090
Do you know
what it brings to my mind?

587
00:41:08.132 --> 00:41:11.678
A hundred sharp little cocks
all vying for attention.

588
00:41:13.304 --> 00:41:15.430
The queen wishes
at the moment

589
00:41:15.431 --> 00:41:17.767
to hear no more petitions.

590
00:41:18.768 --> 00:41:20.269
That is a mistake.

591
00:41:21.187 --> 00:41:22.771
I agree.

592
00:41:22.772 --> 00:41:25.024
There is villainy and violence
on her streets now.

593
00:41:26.943 --> 00:41:28.944
The people are afraid
to go out by night.

594
00:41:28.945 --> 00:41:30.780
It is to her detriment only.

595
00:41:31.698 --> 00:41:33.448
Those who look
to her for relief

596
00:41:33.449 --> 00:41:35.868
now feel she's turned
her back on them.

597
00:41:38.788 --> 00:41:42.624
I wished to hear from you
how you fare in this city.

598
00:41:42.625 --> 00:41:45.460
And if there are others
who may find it a consolation

599
00:41:45.461 --> 00:41:47.546
to come to me
with their troubles

600
00:41:47.547 --> 00:41:49.298
and have them considered.

601
00:41:50.633 --> 00:41:53.635
You make yourself her proxy.

602
00:41:53.636 --> 00:41:55.637
Someone must.
Do you not agree?

603
00:41:55.638 --> 00:41:57.806
If she herself is reluctant.

604
00:41:57.807 --> 00:42:00.934
I can perhaps then bring
certain dilemmas before her

605
00:42:00.935 --> 00:42:04.522
when I judge her mood
to be more accommodating.

606
00:42:07.316 --> 00:42:09.318
You are changed.

607
00:42:12.155 --> 00:42:16.241
This... has changed you.

608
00:42:16.242 --> 00:42:20.037
My heart is with the downtrodden
as it has ever been.

609
00:42:20.038 --> 00:42:21.747
Is it?

610
00:42:21.748 --> 00:42:23.832
Or have you styled yourself
a champion

611
00:42:23.833 --> 00:42:25.543
in order to access these halls?

612
00:42:27.920 --> 00:42:29.005
Look at you.

613
00:42:30.006 --> 00:42:31.506
Standing at the foot
of the throne

614
00:42:31.507 --> 00:42:33.842
wearing a silk worth a year
of my earnings.

615
00:42:33.843 --> 00:42:36.179
promising to whisper
into the ear of a queen.

616
00:42:37.513 --> 00:42:40.515
You thrill now to a tune
you once abhorred.

617
00:42:40.516 --> 00:42:43.268
Does it not occur to you
that from this position

618
00:42:43.269 --> 00:42:45.771
I may help those
who have no avenue?

619
00:42:45.772 --> 00:42:49.025
What power
do you have in truth?

620
00:42:50.443 --> 00:42:52.528
Except to flatter and cajole?

621
00:42:55.782 --> 00:42:56.783
Ah.

622
00:42:57.784 --> 00:42:59.327
Is that why
you called me here?

623
00:43:00.411 --> 00:43:03.372
To look on the trappings so that
someone would hold you in awe?

624
00:43:06.042 --> 00:43:07.627
This was a mistake.

625
00:43:09.087 --> 00:43:11.379
How common
I must seem to you.

626
00:43:11.380 --> 00:43:12.715
That will be all.

627
00:43:15.760 --> 00:43:17.929
Some advice. my lady.

628
00:43:19.263 --> 00:43:21.890
These people
are not your own.

629
00:43:21.891 --> 00:43:23.726
You would do well
to remember that.

630
00:43:25.061 --> 00:43:27.145
Within the walls
of the highborn.

631
00:43:27.146 --> 00:43:31.234
a whore will always and ever
remain a whore.

632
00:43:36.072 --> 00:43:38.074
[footsteps receding]

633
00:43:39.075 --> 00:43:41.118
[dragons bellowing]

634
00:43:41.119 --> 00:43:44.122
[♪ dramatic music playing]

635
00:43:47.125 --> 00:43:49.127
[bellowing continues]

636
00:43:53.756 --> 00:43:55.465
Find her a room.

637
00:43:55.466 --> 00:43:57.093
I do not wish to see her.

638
00:44:03.599 --> 00:44:04.934
[Alicent] Aemond?

639
00:44:08.271 --> 00:44:09.438
Mother.

640
00:44:21.033 --> 00:44:22.617
Your friend Alys.

641
00:44:22.618 --> 00:44:24.328
- She's not my friend.
- Oh.

642
00:44:25.705 --> 00:44:28.039
She doesn't want me
to stay here.

643
00:44:28.040 --> 00:44:30.792
If I'm disturbing
some understanding between--

644
00:44:30.793 --> 00:44:32.127
No.

645
00:44:32.128 --> 00:44:34.212
- I should perhaps not have come.
- No.

646
00:44:34.213 --> 00:44:36.799
I will-- I will take my leave.
if that would behoove you.

647
00:44:38.384 --> 00:44:40.011
I'm glad you came.

648
00:44:43.973 --> 00:44:45.474
I brought you something.

649
00:44:47.226 --> 00:44:48.477
[cup scraping]

650
00:44:51.314 --> 00:44:52.815
Spiced wine.

651
00:44:54.734 --> 00:44:57.653
I remember a time when you would
not fall asleep without it.

652
00:45:04.243 --> 00:45:05.870
Alys doesn't trust you.

653
00:45:14.837 --> 00:45:16.339
Who do you trust?

654
00:45:20.718 --> 00:45:21.719
I...

655
00:45:23.387 --> 00:45:25.264
I tried to kill Aegon.

656
00:45:35.358 --> 00:45:36.442
I know.

657
00:45:39.362 --> 00:45:40.780
[whispering]
My dear...

658
00:45:42.531 --> 00:45:43.950
foolish boy.

659
00:45:55.711 --> 00:45:57.129
Your Grace.

660
00:45:59.215 --> 00:46:00.883
[door opens]

661
00:46:05.054 --> 00:46:06.722
- [door closes]
- No. stay.

662
00:46:22.405 --> 00:46:24.240
She implored me
not to tell you.

663
00:46:31.163 --> 00:46:33.748
She could not face you.
I wished only to protect her.

664
00:46:33.749 --> 00:46:34.916
From what?

665
00:46:34.917 --> 00:46:36.419
What do you think I am?

666
00:46:38.004 --> 00:46:40.422
Y-You are my wife.

667
00:46:40.423 --> 00:46:43.968
She's my daughter.
One I-I-I have long neglected.

668
00:46:47.138 --> 00:46:50.766
Was she not seeking.
in all this.
my favor or yours?

669
00:46:52.977 --> 00:46:57.648
I have looked a hundred times
at that skull you brought...

670
00:46:59.358 --> 00:47:02.194
thinking it was the villain
who killed my son.

671
00:47:06.157 --> 00:47:07.949
I am sorry.

672
00:47:07.950 --> 00:47:10.870
but you must see now that
I kept no scheme against you.

673
00:47:13.205 --> 00:47:15.541
I did only what I thought
was best. Rhaenyra.

674
00:47:20.379 --> 00:47:21.547
Please.

675
00:47:25.468 --> 00:47:26.802
It's late.

676
00:47:43.069 --> 00:47:46.654
[door opens. closes]

677
00:47:46.655 --> 00:47:49.658
[♪ somber music playing]

678
00:48:02.922 --> 00:48:04.340
[whispering] I am sorry.

679
00:48:06.592 --> 00:48:07.885
To Jace.

680
00:48:10.721 --> 00:48:12.514
To you.
You would have been queen.

681
00:48:12.515 --> 00:48:13.848
[Baela] Enough.

682
00:48:13.849 --> 00:48:16.852
[♪ somber music
continues playing]

683
00:48:33.702 --> 00:48:35.204
You will begin anew.

684
00:48:43.045 --> 00:48:46.215
[Alyn] More Hightower
loyalists were found.
Alert the confessors.

685
00:48:50.636 --> 00:48:52.054
[guard] Ser Alyn.

686
00:48:53.305 --> 00:48:54.598
It was left for you.

687
00:49:09.280 --> 00:49:11.739
[breathing shakily]

688
00:49:11.740 --> 00:49:13.075
[owl screeching]

689
00:49:14.285 --> 00:49:16.287
[bird squawking]

690
00:49:26.338 --> 00:49:28.131
[thud]

691
00:49:28.132 --> 00:49:29.133
Alys.

692
00:49:33.679 --> 00:49:34.930
Idiot.

693
00:49:37.766 --> 00:49:40.769
[♪ dramatic music playing]

694
00:50:06.629 --> 00:50:08.964
[screaming]

695
00:50:11.467 --> 00:50:13.469
[baby crying]

696
00:50:19.391 --> 00:50:21.393
[baby continues crying]

697
00:50:25.898 --> 00:50:26.982
[whimpers]

698
00:50:30.986 --> 00:50:32.154
[gasps]

699
00:50:35.407 --> 00:50:37.409
[Dreamfyre chirping]

700
00:50:40.913 --> 00:50:42.665
[snarling and screeching]

701
00:50:45.501 --> 00:50:47.336
<i>Dracarys!</i>

702
00:50:53.050 --> 00:50:55.176
[chickens clucking]

703
00:50:55.177 --> 00:50:58.180
[♪ gentle music playing]

704
00:51:05.688 --> 00:51:07.690
[wind whistling]

705
00:51:14.738 --> 00:51:16.740
[distorted noises intensifying]

706
00:51:22.037 --> 00:51:24.039
[fire crackling softly]

707
00:51:29.295 --> 00:51:32.298
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

708
00:51:46.979 --> 00:51:48.731
[bones rattling]

709
00:51:52.943 --> 00:51:55.904
[Rhaenyra] <i>It was Rhaena
he was hiding all along.</i>

710
00:51:58.782 --> 00:52:01.242
He lied.
I did not lead you astray.

711
00:52:01.243 --> 00:52:03.995
And yet you cannot say
he betrayed me

712
00:52:03.996 --> 00:52:06.414
so much as he would not
betray his daughter.

713
00:52:06.415 --> 00:52:07.832
This time.

714
00:52:07.833 --> 00:52:10.752
But does it not prove
he is willing to deceive you

715
00:52:10.753 --> 00:52:12.630
- if he judges it necessary?
- [scoffs]

716
00:52:13.464 --> 00:52:15.506
And you've never done the same?

717
00:52:15.507 --> 00:52:17.592
I've acted only
in your interests.

718
00:52:17.593 --> 00:52:19.762
You have sought
to turn me from him.

719
00:52:20.846 --> 00:52:24.807
Pouring your honey in my ear.
whispering. encouraging.

720
00:52:24.808 --> 00:52:27.143
seeking to make me
in your image.

721
00:52:27.144 --> 00:52:28.853
In my image?

722
00:52:28.854 --> 00:52:32.106
Your Grace. have I ever
counseled you to do aught

723
00:52:32.107 --> 00:52:35.318
but what Viserys
would have you do in his place?

724
00:52:35.319 --> 00:52:37.987
As you have ofttimes said.
is your own desire.

725
00:52:37.988 --> 00:52:41.325
Yes. and in hewing
to his vision.
what have I reaped?

726
00:52:42.284 --> 00:52:44.452
Peace?
Prosperity?

727
00:52:44.453 --> 00:52:46.789
Ah. the gratitude
of my subjects.

728
00:52:54.880 --> 00:52:56.632
My father was not a dreamer.

729
00:52:58.133 --> 00:52:59.968
But his whole life
was a dream.

730
00:53:03.555 --> 00:53:05.140
Do not lose faith.

731
00:53:06.975 --> 00:53:09.978
You are on the precipice
of a great victory.

732
00:53:11.980 --> 00:53:14.148
The uncertainties
that oppress you

733
00:53:14.149 --> 00:53:15.651
will soon be resolved.

734
00:53:16.652 --> 00:53:20.155
Those who oppose you
will fall away.

735
00:53:21.573 --> 00:53:24.909
Even Aemond
is all but vanquished.

736
00:53:24.910 --> 00:53:28.247
You will be queen
for many years after this.

737
00:53:29.248 --> 00:53:31.667
And your children's children
after you.

738
00:53:36.839 --> 00:53:38.674
Just a little longer.

739
00:53:44.012 --> 00:53:45.222
Do you think...

740
00:53:46.682 --> 00:53:47.850
I am worthy?

741
00:53:50.519 --> 00:53:52.563
In this moment. my queen.

742
00:53:56.024 --> 00:53:57.609
Rhaenyra.

743
00:54:05.868 --> 00:54:08.203
I have never been
more certain of it.

744
00:54:13.542 --> 00:54:16.545
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

745
00:55:03.175 --> 00:55:06.178
[faint rhythmic beating]

746
00:55:15.938 --> 00:55:17.940
[faint beating continues]

747
00:55:27.282 --> 00:55:29.284
[beating grows louder]

748
00:55:31.453 --> 00:55:34.164
A final stand then.
Ser Tyland.

749
00:55:35.916 --> 00:55:37.376
Your Grace.

750
00:56:05.863 --> 00:56:10.409
We claim this land for Rhaenyra.
Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

751
00:56:11.660 --> 00:56:13.911
You will throw down your arms

752
00:56:13.912 --> 00:56:16.206
and make ready
to swear your fealty.

753
00:56:21.336 --> 00:56:23.754
[softly]
Oh. no. no. no. no. no.

754
00:56:23.755 --> 00:56:24.840
[Tyland] Your Grace?

755
00:56:26.758 --> 00:56:28.176
Will you flee after all?

756
00:56:45.819 --> 00:56:48.613
We shall not surrender
to the false queen.

757
00:56:48.614 --> 00:56:50.616
[laughter]

758
00:56:56.872 --> 00:56:59.041
Is that you.
Tyland Lannister?

759
00:56:59.958 --> 00:57:01.877
Your queen's been
looking for you.

760
00:57:03.712 --> 00:57:05.963
Tell us where the gold is.

761
00:57:05.964 --> 00:57:09.051
and you will die
with your ears still attached.

762
00:57:22.648 --> 00:57:24.316
Behold me now!

763
00:57:25.233 --> 00:57:26.776
[horse whinnying]

764
00:57:26.777 --> 00:57:28.737
I am Aegon Targaryen!

765
00:57:30.405 --> 00:57:32.949
- Viserys' true heir!
- [distant bellowing]

766
00:57:32.950 --> 00:57:36.661
The sixth King of the Andals
and the Rhoynar

767
00:57:36.662 --> 00:57:38.245
and the First Men!

768
00:57:38.246 --> 00:57:41.165
I was anointed
by the High Septon

769
00:57:41.166 --> 00:57:43.125
in the light of the Seven.

770
00:57:43.126 --> 00:57:47.339
And it is in their light
that I stand before you now!

771
00:57:49.257 --> 00:57:51.592
Strike me down!

772
00:57:51.593 --> 00:57:54.763
And the Stranger
will take retribution.

773
00:57:56.306 --> 00:57:59.934
The Warrior's sword
will be judgment upon you.

774
00:57:59.935 --> 00:58:02.186
[dragon snarling]

775
00:58:02.187 --> 00:58:04.480
[chuckles] Yes.

776
00:58:04.481 --> 00:58:06.608
Yes. cowards.

777
00:58:07.484 --> 00:58:09.443
- You might well retreat.
- [rumbling]

778
00:58:09.444 --> 00:58:12.363
For now you see me
as I truly am!

779
00:58:12.364 --> 00:58:13.823
- [dragon snarling]
- [gasping softly]

780
00:58:13.824 --> 00:58:16.158
Dreadful in vengeance!

781
00:58:16.159 --> 00:58:19.371
- Righteous and glorious!
- [horses whinnying]

782
00:58:22.499 --> 00:58:24.501
[dragon bellowing
and growling]

783
00:58:26.545 --> 00:58:28.547
[dragon chirping]

784
00:58:30.465 --> 00:58:31.842
[whispering] Sunfyre.

785
00:58:34.136 --> 00:58:36.138
[Sunfyre chittering]

786
00:58:39.141 --> 00:58:40.475
Sunfyre.

787
00:58:42.144 --> 00:58:43.729
<i>Dracarys.</i>

788
00:58:45.647 --> 00:58:48.066
Run! Save yourselves!

789
00:58:49.151 --> 00:58:51.153
[soldiers screaming]

790
00:58:53.864 --> 00:58:55.866
[Aegon yelling]

791
00:58:57.200 --> 00:58:59.202
[screaming continues]

792
00:59:01.997 --> 00:59:03.999
[Aegon continues yelling]

793
00:59:09.004 --> 00:59:11.048
[Aegon laughing]

794
00:59:16.887 --> 00:59:19.014
[bellowing]

795
00:59:28.190 --> 00:59:29.357
Oh.

796
00:59:31.902 --> 00:59:33.236
Decent ale. that.

797
00:59:35.739 --> 00:59:37.282
I thought you might enjoy it.

798
00:59:42.037 --> 00:59:44.748
- [gulping] Mm.
- I have had word...

799
00:59:45.916 --> 00:59:49.960
since we last spoke
of a most distressing incident.

800
00:59:49.961 --> 00:59:53.215
My whisperers tell me that
Daemon Targaryen struck you.

801
00:59:54.382 --> 00:59:55.759
In the street.

802
00:59:57.969 --> 01:00:00.972
In front of all the commoners
passing by.

803
01:00:02.140 --> 01:00:06.228
An intolerable insult
to someone of your stature.

804
01:00:08.230 --> 01:00:12.566
But then. uh. it's almost to be
expected from those people.

805
01:00:12.567 --> 01:00:14.402
She did tell me
not to go into town.

806
01:00:15.237 --> 01:00:17.071
- To be fair.
- Ludicrous.

807
01:00:17.072 --> 01:00:19.241
A man needs his sustenance
and cheer.

808
01:00:21.368 --> 01:00:24.328
But it is obvious
Rhaenyra and her ilk

809
01:00:24.329 --> 01:00:25.789
regard you only as a tool.

810
01:00:27.749 --> 01:00:30.127
To be used and reprimanded.

811
01:00:32.587 --> 01:00:34.422
Whereas I understand...

812
01:00:35.924 --> 01:00:37.300
who you really are.

813
01:00:42.764 --> 01:00:45.100
You said last time...

814
01:00:47.185 --> 01:00:49.146
that you could give me
a lordship.

815
01:00:51.273 --> 01:00:52.607
And a castle.

816
01:00:54.609 --> 01:00:55.694
Honeyholt.

817
01:00:57.529 --> 01:00:58.697
Honeyholt?

818
01:00:59.990 --> 01:01:02.450
[chuckles]
Honeyholt is a trifle.

819
01:01:04.161 --> 01:01:06.829
It seems that
Driftmark itself

820
01:01:06.830 --> 01:01:08.623
may soon be without a master.

821
01:01:10.458 --> 01:01:12.627
Lord of the Tides.

822
01:01:14.629 --> 01:01:16.298
What do you think of that?

823
01:01:22.804 --> 01:01:24.638
- [chuckles]
- [mugs clanking]

824
01:01:24.639 --> 01:01:26.474
They will laugh
at you no more...

825
01:01:27.559 --> 01:01:29.311
when they see you as you are.

826
01:01:33.565 --> 01:01:34.733
No.

827
01:01:36.818 --> 01:01:38.153
They will burn.

828
01:01:49.039 --> 01:01:51.833
♪
